{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>So the children of Gad and the children of Reuben came</b> – Scripture placed the children of Reuben first in the first verse, \"And a great multitude of cattle belonged to the children of Reuben and the children of Gad,\" according to proper order, for he is the firstborn and the son of the matriarch. And so too when Scripture recounts this matter it says: \"And to the Reubenite and to the Gadite I gave\" (Deuteronomy 3:16). But in this entire passage Scripture places the children of Gad first, for they gave this counsel and they were the ones who spoke first to Moses concerning this inheritance, and they were mightier than the children of Reuben, as it says: \"and he tears the arm, even the crown of the head\" (Deuteronomy 33:20). And therefore they were not afraid to dwell alone in this land because of the inhabitants of the land. Now Moses suspected them of saying this out of fear of the people of the land of Canaan, as the spies had said of them: \"We are not able to go up against the people, for they are stronger than we\" (Numbers 13:31). And therefore he said to them that they do not trust in HaShem as their fathers did, and he further sought to punish them likewise by leaving them in the wilderness. And so they answered him: Far be it that we fear them; rather, we will cross over armed for battle and we will be swift and first before the people to fight the enemies of HaShem, for they are our bread!"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:59.306425193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}